    "problem": "Global climate models, due to their coarse resolution, are not expected to represent extreme weather events with the same intensity and frequency as observed data, creating uncertainty about the plausibility of their simulations, particularly for precipitation-related events.",
    "method": "This study compares observed and modeled trends of three climate extreme indices in South America to analyze the reliability of IPCC-AR4 global models in simulating historical extremes during 1960-2000.",
    "task": "The task is to compare observed and modeled historical trends of extreme temperature and rainfall events over South America during the last half of the twentieth century to analyze the reliability of global climate models.",
